`reminder_text(appointment)` already exists in `src/slotwise/reminders.py`, so I made no changes. It was added in commit `e503db3`, and the working tree is clean.

I ran `tests/test_reminders.py`: all 8 tests pass. A sample reminder for Zoë Brändli with Lena at 09:00 on 7 Sep 2026 reads:

`Lindqvist Physio: Hi Zoe, reminder of your appointment with Lena on Mon 07 Sep at 09:00. To move it, call 044 512 77 30.`

The function:
- raises `ValueError` for cancelled appointments;
- converts the text to plain ASCII (umlauts to German spellings, other accents stripped);
- raises `ValueError` if the text is over 160 characters rather than splitting it;
- includes the reception number `044 512 77 30`.

The sender "Lindqvist Physio" and the greeting "Hi <first name>," are still my choices, which reception has not confirmed. Choosing which appointments get a reminder and when is not built yet.
